# Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)

- Keep interfaces small and role-specific.
- Avoid forcing consumers to depend on methods they do not use.
- Split broad contracts into focused interfaces/protocols.
- Prefer multiple narrow abstractions over one “god interface”.

## Review checklist

- Does any consumer implement/receive methods it does not need?
- Can this contract be split by usage context?
- Are dependencies minimized per caller role?
